# kton binaries are not published here - build them from the plankton repo (see README)
bin/plankton
bin/nekton
bin/kton
# private key material must NEVER be committed to a public repo (belt-and-suspenders: keep this even
# though each example writes its keys under .work/keys/, which we otherwise now PERSIST - see below)
*.key
*.pem
# Each example PERSISTS its .work/ so every foton's recorded input/output path is a real, fetchable
# file in this repo (its raw permalink is the FileRef's carried `uri`). So .work/ is NOT ignored
# wholesale - but only the DATA in it earns its place in the index. What a run DERIVES is ignored:
#
#   the registries, the public keys and the signed envelopes are rewritten on every single run, with a
#   fresh keypair each time and (for `nekton seed`/`annotate` records) a wall-clock `when`, so they can
#   never diff cleanly. They were 219 of the 353 tracked .work/ files and 219 of the 255 that changed
#   on every full run - noise that buried the real diffs. Nothing points at them: not one of them is
#   the target of a carried `uri`, which is the only reason .work/ is tracked at all.
#
# bin/check-permalinks.py enforces the half that matters - every carried permalink must resolve to a
# tracked file - so if a future example locates a file these rules exclude, CI says so instead of
# publishing a record whose `uri` quietly 404s.
**/.work/**/objects/**
**/.work/**/*.pub
**/.work/**/*.dsse.json
**/.work/**/*.foton.json
# The same reasoning for the other things a run manufactures rather than starts from: the claim specs
# it prints on the fly (they carry the run's keyids), the RDF it exports, and the record dumps the
# checks read. All regenerated, none the target of a carried `uri`.
**/.work/**/*.spec.json
**/.work/**/*.trig
**/.work/**/*.ttl
**/.work/**/*.jsonl
**/.work/**/exports/**
**/.work/**/rec.json
**/.work/**/*.err

# Scratch/draft material under docs/ - never committed. (docs/findings.md is the one working
# note we DO want tracked, so it's deliberately not listed here.)
/docs/examplesTest/
/docs/show-hn-kton.md
